## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a space, add and remove an object
  desc: The core space round-trip — create a space, add an object to it, remove it with undo data.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-1.1, F-3.1, T-1, T-3]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - no space named "QA Space" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the space
      do: Click "New space" in the sidebar and name it "QA Space".
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.Create] { name: "QA Space" }
      capture: created
      expect: a new space named "QA Space" exists and opens in the navtree
      assert: return $created.space.properties.name === 'QA Space';
    - name: Create a collection to add to
      do: In "QA Space", click + and choose Collection. Name it "QA Collection".
      invoke: [op:CollectionOperation.Create] { name: "QA Collection" }
      capture: collection
      expect: a Collection named "QA Collection" exists in the space
      assert: return $collection.object.name === 'QA Collection';
    - name: Add an object to the space
      do: In the navtree, click + on "QA Collection" and choose Markdown. Name it "QA Doc".
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.markdown.create { name: "QA Doc" }
      capture: doc
      expect: a Document named "QA Doc" now exists
    - name: Place it in the collection
      do: (the navtree create action places it for you)
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddObject] { object: $doc.object, target: $collection.object }
      capture: added
      expect: "QA Doc" appears as a row under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $collection.object.objects.some((ref) => ref.target?.id === $doc.object.id);
      note: Coalesced with the previous step — `doc.object` is live and cannot cross a snippet boundary.
    - name: Remove the object
      do: Right-click "QA Doc" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.RemoveObjects] { objects: [$doc.object], target: $collection.object }
      capture: removed
      expect: "QA Doc" leaves the navtree row list under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $removed.objects.some((o) => o.id === $doc.object.id);
    - name: Restore the object
      do: Undo the delete (Cmd/Ctrl+Z), or use the undo toast.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.RestoreObjects] { objects: $removed.objects, parentCollection: $removed.parentCollection, indices: $removed.indices, wasActive: $removed.wasActive }
      expect: "QA Doc" reappears as a row under "QA Collection"
      assert: return $collection.object.objects.some((ref) => ref.target?.id === $doc.object.id);
  after:
    - name: Delete the space
      do: Right-click "QA Space" in the sidebar and choose Delete Space.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.delete { space: $created.space }
      expect: "QA Space" no longer appears in the sidebar
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Register a schema and add a typed relation
  desc: Schema-registry and relation round-trip — the machinery plugin-table/plugin-kanban build on.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-4.1, T-5]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no schema typename "example.org/type/QaThing" is already registered in the space — ABORT
      rather than reusing a registration this test did not create
    - schema: a runtime `Schema.Struct` for typename "example.org/type/QaThing" to register
    - relationSchema: a runtime relation schema (source/target typed) to link `a` and `b` with
    - a: an object already in the space, the relation's source
    - b: an object already in the space, the relation's target
  steps:
    - name: Register the schema
      do: Open Settings -> Schema for the space and register a new type, or create an object of a
        new type from the type picker, which registers it implicitly.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddSchema] { db: $given.space.db, typename: "example.org/type/QaThing", schema: $given.schema, show: true }
      capture: registered
      expect: the type appears in the space's schema registry and in the create-object type picker
      assert: return $registered.object.typename === 'example.org/type/QaThing';
    - name: Add a typed relation between two objects
      do: With two objects selected, use the relation-creation affordance to link them with the
        registered relation schema.
      invoke: [op:SpaceOperation.AddRelation] { db: $given.space.db, schema: $given.relationSchema, source: $given.a, target: $given.b }
      expect: a relation now exists linking the two objects, visible wherever relations render
      assert: return !!$result.relation;
  after:
    - name: No teardown
      do: Schema registrations are not removed by this test — they are lightweight and harmless
        to leave in a scratch space.
      expect: the space still opens cleanly and the registered schemas remain listed
```

```mdl
test QA-3: Share one document of a space with a fresh browser
  desc: Object sharing end to end — the link joins a guest with no identity and replicates only what the shared document needs.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-2.5, F-2.6, F-2.7, F-2.8]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - host: a booted app with an identity and a space holding ten documents, one of which links to another
    - guest: a SECOND, fresh browser profile with no identity
  steps:
    - name: Open the share dialog
      do: On the host, open the linking document and click Share in its heading.
      expect: the dialog lists the host under People with access, General access reads Anyone with the link, and it names the two documents the link shares
    - name: Copy the link
      do: Click Copy link.
      expect: the link appears in the dialog and is copied
    - name: Open the link on the guest
      do: Paste the link into the guest's address bar.
      expect: the guest gets an identity with no welcome screen, joins the space, and shows the shared document's text
    - name: Follow the link inside the document
      do: On the guest, follow the shared document's link to the other document.
      expect: the linked document opens
  then:
    - the guest holds the two shared documents and the space properties, and none of the other eight documents
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Every object in Composer has a Share button that opens a share dialog laid out like Google Docs' and built from the Composer design-system primitives.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.5, op:SpaceOperation.OpenShareObject]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: Sharing an object creates a link that carries a delegated invitation (created automatically), the plugins needed to render the object, and the subset of the space to synchronize: the object and all its children.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.6, op:SpaceOperation.ShareObject]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Opening a share link loads the object for a member; joins a non-member in the background, enables the plugins and synchronizes only the shared subset, guarded on the client; and creates an identity in place for a browser with none.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.7, F-2.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The partial-sync guard is client-side only, and the spec says so; EDGE does not restrict a member to a subset of the space's documents.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.8]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A link's scope is the object, every object reachable through its references or through ECHO links in its text, and the space properties; the root collection is left out. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.6]
  why: A document that links another must open with its link working, and the space does not report ready without its properties. The root collection would list every object in the space as an unloadable reference.
  rejected:
    - References only — a markdown link to another document would open nothing on the guest.
```

```mdl
decision D-6: The link is the object's shareable path plus a `share` query parameter, so a member opens it through the existing URL projection. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.6, F-2.7]
  why: Members need no new code path; only a non-member reads the payload.
  rejected:
    - A dedicated share route — every member would pay a redirect, and it duplicates object routing.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: The guard quarantines out-of-scope documents with an `out-of-scope` reason and leaves them out of the space's collection; a stored `sync_scope` in the space metadata re-applies it on every start. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.8]
  why: The quarantine already refuses a document on load, request, accept, serve and advertise, so one more reason covers every direction at once.
  rejected:
    - A separate allow-list gate — it would duplicate every quarantine call site.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The link uses a delegated, multi-use invitation authenticated by a known public key, with the role from the dialog (Editor or Viewer). Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.6, op:SpaceOperation.ShareObject]
  why: It is the invitation the existing invite-many link uses, which EDGE already redeems with no member online.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: A link's scope is the object, every object reachable through its references or through ECHO links in its text, the space properties, and each scoped object's strong dependencies — its parent and a type stored in the space — whose own references are not followed. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  supersedes: D-5
  affects: [F-2.6]
  why: The host index and the client both hide an object whose strong dependency is missing, so a document filed in the root collection opened on the guest as a plank that never left loading. Following a dependency's references would replicate every sibling of the shared document.
  rejected:
    - Leave the root collection out ([D-5]) — the shared document never surfaced on the guest.
    - Follow the dependencies' references too — sharing one document would replicate its whole collection.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: With the Viewer role selected, the share dialog says that Viewer is not enforced and anyone with the link can still edit. Fills in [D-8].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:mykola-vrmchk
  affects: [F-2.5]
  why: The role is recorded on the member credential but nothing checks it on a write, so a Viewer link grants edit access; the dialog must not imply otherwise.
  rejected:
    - Hide the Viewer option until enforcement exists — drops the Google-Docs layout the dialog follows, and the role is still recorded for when it is enforced.
```

---

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap
    literals?: UnionList
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap
    state?: FieldMap
    slots?: FieldMap
    actions?: ActionMap
    emits?: EventMap
    layout?: CodeBlock
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap
    output?: TypeExpr
    errors?: ErrorMap
    effects?: EffectList
    requires?: ServiceList
    note?: Prose
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains, e.g. [Scene, F-2.1]
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
